Subject: [PATCH] al-sap: retry registration during 1905 startup

The em_ctrl service waits for the ieee1905 Unix socket pathname, but a
pathname can outlive its listener and ieee1905's forking service can report
started before it accepts connections.  AlServiceAccessPoint then throws
ConnectionFailed from its constructor and the uncaught exception terminates
the EasyMesh process with SIGABRT.

Retry the existing registration transaction for a bounded 90 seconds in both
controller and agent.  Delete a partially constructed SAP between attempts,
and return a normal startup error rather than producing a core dump when the
dependency never becomes ready.

Upstream-Status: Pending
